# sdftorgb

- Label: SDF to RGB
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 59 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/sdftorgb.html
- Summary (EN): SDF to RGB converts a 2D signed distance field into an RGB colour layer. It draws the shape, outline and shadow that the field defines, with colours set by parameters or colour ramps.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud SDF to RGB transforme un champ de distance signé 2D en couche RGB, avec la forme, le contour et l'ombre qu'il définit.

- Inputs meaning: ["sdf: the SDF mono layer to convert; the output is one rgb layer"]

- Key parameters: ["Background: Background Color, Iso Range, Color Ramp", "Shape: Draw Shape, Shape Color, Iso Distance, Color Ramp", "Outline: Draw Outline, Outline Color, Outline Width, Alignment (inside, outside or centered)", "Shadowing: Draw Shadowing, Shadow Density, Shadow Falloff, Shadow Color", "SDF: Iso Value (higher values enlarge the shape), Onion Skin, Smooth, Anti-Aliasing, Invert"]

- Caveats: ["The page lists no specific limitations", "The input must be a mono SDF layer; ramp remapping applies only when a colour menu is set to Use Ramp"]

